div.verse:
To be humble above all men; to reverence the aged; to labour to be righteous;  
            συντηρειν. to respect the brotherhood; to bear affronts; to be long-suffering;  
            Add from the Gr. of Athanasius and Antiochus: Not to remember injuries; To comfort those who labour in their minds. not to cast away those that have fallen from the faith, but to convert them, and make them be of  
            Ευθυμους. good cheer; to admonish sinners; not to oppress those that are our debtors; and all other things of a like kind.

For all these that are about the tower must be cleansed, lest the master of the house chance to come upon the sudden, and find those which are about the tower unclean;  
            MS. Lamb. Ita exasperetur, ut hi lapides. and be so exasperated, that these stones should never be put into the building of this tower, and I shall be looked upon to have been  
            MS. Lamb. Negligens, patrisfamilias. unmindful of my master's commands.

Hear, said he, O foolish man! and understand. The Son of God is indeed more ancient than any creature;  
            Ita ut. Lat. insomuch that he was in council with his Father at the creation of  
            The creatures. all things.

MS. Lamb. Et unum quemque spiritum fleri: which appears from the Gr. of Antiochus to be the true reading, και γενεσθαι εν πνευμα. But become one spirit, and provide remedies for these evil rents, and remove them from you; that the lord of the sheep may rejoice  
MS. Lamb. Gaudeat de his; and Gr. Antioch χαρη επ αυτω. at it;  
Vid. Antioch. Hom. cxxii. for he will rejoice, if he shall find all whole.
